  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Testosterone, which is a steroidal hormone, has the following structure.</p><p><img height=\"209\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/8108b3aa-1ce8-4c2b-af93-0b7d3ab52086-image.png\" width=\"320\" /></p><p>The total number of asymmetric carbon atom/s in testosterone is ____________.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>A chiral center (Asymmetric&nbsp;center) of an atom is the atom in a molecule that is bonded to four different chemical species. The chemical species is an atom/molecule with a specific molecular structure. In the following molecule, chiral carbon are marked with &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>*</mo></math>&#39;.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6dc3ab38-9b1c-4c31-b8ea-8fabdb012252-image.png\" style=\"width: 280px; height: 224px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
